    "objectives": "# Scenario 5 — Multiple changes with scheduling conflicts\n\n## Context\nThe patient's psychiatrist has recommended adding a group social activity on Monday and Wednesday afternoons to help with depression. Additionally, the physiotherapy session on Mondays needs to be moved earlier to accommodate a new transport schedule.\n\n## Objectives\n1. Move the physiotherapy session (ph_001) on Mondays from 10:00 to 09:00.\n2. Add a new social activity called 'Group social hour', 60 minutes, every Monday and Wednesday at 15:00.\n3. If the assistant detects any conflict with existing activities or medications, follow its suggestions for resolving them.\n4. Once both changes are confirmed, end the conversation.\n\n## Notes\n- Address the objectives in order: first the physiotherapy update, then the new social activity.\n- If the assistant raises concerns about the patient's Parkinson's or Depression medications interacting with the new schedule, acknowledge the concerns and defer to the assistant's recommendations.\n- The scenario is considered fully successful only if both changes are confirmed by the assistant."
